(TaskRunner pid=[process]) [response] We are given the following information:
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - Aya walks **9 km** each morning.
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - She walks at a constant speed of **$ s $ km/h**.
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - The total time for the walk (including the **$ t $ minutes** spent in the coffee shop) is **4 hours**.
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - When she walks at **$ s + 2 $ km/h**, the total time is **2 hours and 24 minutes** (i.e., $ 2 + \frac{24}{60} = 2.4 $ hours).
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - We are to find the **time** it takes her to walk **$ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h**, including the $ t $ minutes.
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) ---
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) ### Step 1: Set up the equations
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) Let’s define the total time for the walk (including the $ t $ minutes) in hours.
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) #### Case 1: Speed $ s $ km/h
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - Time = $ \frac{9}{s} $ hours
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - Total time = $ \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 $ hours
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) #### Case 2: Speed $ s + 2 $ km/h
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - Time = $ \frac{9}{s + 2} $ hours
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - Total time = $ \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2.4 $ hours
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) ---
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) ### Step 2: Solve the two equations
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) #### From Case 1:
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 \tag{1}
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) #### From Case 2:
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2.4 \tag{2}
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) Subtract equation (1) from equation (2):
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) \left( \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} \right) - \left( \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} \right) = 2.4 - 4
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) \frac{9}{s + 2} - \frac{9}{s} = -1.6
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 9 \left( \frac{1}{s + 2} - \frac{1}{s} \right) = -1.6
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 9 \left( \frac{s - (s + 2)}{s(s + 2)} \right) = -1.6
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 9 \left( \frac{-2}{s(s + 2)} \right) = -1.6
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) - \frac{18}{s(s + 2)} = -1.6
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) \frac{18}{s(s + 2)} = 1.6
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) s(s + 2) = \frac{18}{1.6} = 11.25 \tag{3}
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) $$
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) ---
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) ### Step 3: Solve for $ s $
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) 
(TaskRunner pid=[process]) We now solve the quadratic equation:
